  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.7.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: merman-cli\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/Latias94/merman/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: e1d787154be74bca8262cc9c83ee3cb3f7e0c13dd4b8eb65c41cb2e42d3b5092\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    env:\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO: fat\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n    content:\n      - cd crates/merman-cli\n      - if: unix\n        then:\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"$PREFIX\" --no-track --locked --bins\n      - if: win\n        then:\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\" --no-track --locked --bins\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format=yaml --output=../../THIRDPARTY.yml\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - merman-cli --help\n      - merman-cli --version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - merman-cli\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: Mermaid.js, but headless, in Rust. Parse, layout and render diagrams to SVG/PNG/JPG/PDF/ASCII/Unicode.\n  description: |\n    `merman-cli` is a performant browserless Mermaid command-line renderer in Rust for SVG, PNG, JPG, PDF, and\n    ASCII/Unicode text output. The top-level command follows common `mmdc` workflows, while developer subcommands\n    expose merman's parse, layout, and render internals.\n  license: MIT OR Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE-MIT\n    - LICENSE-APACHE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  homepage: https://github.com/Latias94/merman\n  repository: https://github.com/Latias94/merman\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - salim-b\n",
